        <briefdescription>
<para>Abort an interruptible public-key export operation. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>This is a beta API, and thus subject to change at any point. It is not bound by the usual interface stability promises.</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>This function clears the number of ops completed as part of the operation. Please ensure you copy this value via <computeroutput><ref refid="group__interruptible__export__public__key_1ga110fa7d47ea47b5c3fd7e3f649244d0d" kindref="member">psa_export_public_key_iop_get_num_ops()</ref></computeroutput> if required before calling.</para><simplesectsep/><para>Aborting an operation frees all associated resources except for the operation structure itself. Once aborted, the operation object can be reused for another operation by calling <computeroutput><ref refid="group__interruptible__export__public__key_1ga9c0c35ea5b242b4161295d07f27a293a" kindref="member">psa_export_public_key_iop_setup()</ref></computeroutput> again.</para><simplesectsep/><para>You may call this function any time after the operation object has been initialized. In particular, calling <computeroutput><ref refid="group__interruptible__export__public__key_1ga66799e49ee4be8cb3f49c910e8fba64b" kindref="member">psa_export_public_key_iop_abort()</ref></computeroutput> after the operation has already been terminated by a call to <computeroutput><ref refid="group__interruptible__export__public__key_1ga66799e49ee4be8cb3f49c910e8fba64b" kindref="member">psa_export_public_key_iop_abort()</ref></computeroutput> or <computeroutput><ref refid="group__interruptible__export__public__key_1gaf1c95a0c9d3db461ba582b278d27e7bc" kindref="member">psa_export_public_key_iop_complete()</ref></computeroutput> is safe.</para></simplesect>
